        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Right shoulder pain"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Dull ache in the lateral right shoulder and upper arm, increased by reaching overhead or out to the side; night pain, especially when lying on the right side, waking the patient a few times per week. No trauma, fall, or heavy lifting; possible overreach into a cupboard and sleeping in a recliner. Patient describes the arm as more weak than painful. Pain and weakness affect lifting a jug and shopping; struggles above shoulder height and uses the left hand to assist. Dressing, putting on a bra or jumper, washing hair, and hanging washing are slower; avoids overhead tasks but remains independent. Today describes the shoulder as just a bit weak and a bit sore."
      }
    },
